        "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<title>Davenport Brothers Farewell Tour Poster</title>\n<style>\n    body {\n        margin: 0;\n        padding: 20px;\n        background-color: #e0e0e0;\n        display: flex;\n        justify-content: center;\n        font-family: \"Times New Roman\", Times, serif;\n        color: #111;\n    }\n    .poster-container {\n        background-color: #fff;\n        max-width: 750px;\n        width: 100%;\n        padding: 40px 50px;\n        box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);\n        box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n    .text-center { text-align: center; }\n    \n    .plate { font-size: 16px; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 20px; }\n    .st-james { font-family: \"Arial Black\", sans-serif; font-size: 46px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 10px; }\n    .date-line { font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 15px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }\n    \n    .divider {\n        border: none;\n        border-top: 3px solid #000;\n        border-bottom: 1px solid #000;\n        height: 2px;\n        margin: 15px 0;\n    }\n    \n    .farewell { font-size: 24px; letter-spacing: 14px; margin-top: 15px; margin-bottom: 5px; }\n    .absence { font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 15px; }\n    \n    .ira { font-family: \"Georgia\", serif; font-size: 52px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-bottom: 5px; transform: scaleY(1.1); display: inline-block; }\n    .survivor { font-size: 13px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: 3px; margin-bottom: 5px; }\n    \n    .brothers { font-family: \"Impact\", \"Arial Narrow\", sans-serif; font-size: 80px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: -1px; transform: scaleY(1.3); margin-bottom: 30px; margin-top: 10px; display: block; }\n    \n    .and-line { font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 8px; margin-bottom: 10px; }\n    \n    .prof-day { font-family: \"Georgia\", serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 5px; margin-bottom: 15px; }\n    .departure { font-size: 16px; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 25px; }\n    \n    .placeholder {\n        width: 100%;\n        height: 420px;\n        border: 2px dashed #888;\n        background-color: #f5f5f5;\n        display: flex;\n        align-items: center;\n        justify-content: center;\n        margin-bottom: 25px;\n        font-family: sans-serif;\n        color: #555;\n        font-size: 14px;\n        text-align: center;\n        padding: 20px;\n        box-sizing: border-box;\n    }\n    \n    .unique { font-size: 20px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: 4px; word-spacing: 6px; margin-bottom: 10px; }\n    \n    .text-block { font-size: 12.5px; text-align: left; line-height: 1.25; margin-bottom: 10px; }\n    .indent { display: inline-block; width: 25px; }\n    .large-space { display: inline-block; width: 40px; }\n    \n    .powers-container { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin: 10px 0; gap: 10px; }\n    .powers-text { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 6px; }\n    .hand { font-size: 30px; }\n    \n    .challenge { font-family: \"Arial Black\", sans-serif; font-size: 36px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 12px; margin: 15px 0; }\n    .light { font-family: \"Arial Black\", sans-serif; font-size: 34px; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 16px; margin: 15px 0; }\n    \n    .caption { font-size: 14px; font-variant: small-caps; text-align: center; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 35px; padding: 0 10px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<div class=\"poster-container\">\n    <div class=\"plate text-center\">PLATE 5.</div>\n    <div class=\"st-james text-center\">ST. JAMES HALL,</div>\n    <div class=\"date-line text-center\">ON SUNDAY EVENING, FEBRUARY 23d, 1879.</div>\n    \n    <hr class=\"divider\">\n    \n    <div class=\"farewell text-center\">FAREWELL TOUR!</div>\n    <div class=\"absence text-center\">AFTER SIX YEARS ABSENCE IN FOREIGN COUNTRIES,</div>\n    \n    <div class=\"text-center\"><span class=\"ira\">IRA E. DAVENPORT</span></div>\n    <div class=\"survivor text-center\">Survivor of the World Renowned</div>\n    <div class=\"text-center\"><span class=\"brothers\">DAVENPORT BROTHERS</span></div>\n    \n    <div class=\"and-line text-center\">— AND —</div>\n    \n    <div class=\"prof-day text-center\">PROF. J. F. DAY</div>\n    <div class=\"departure text-center\">Previous to their departure to Mexico and South America.</div>\n    \n    <div class=\"placeholder\">\n        [Illustration: Magical performance scene. Three bound men sitting on chairs. Above them, ghostly hands float, and various musical instruments (guitars, violins, horns) are suspended in mid-air. Two standing men observe the scene on the left and right edges.]\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"unique text-center\">In Unique and Startling Wonders!</div>\n    \n    <div class=\"text-block\">\n        Mysterious displays, and unaccountable Mysteries, which have been given in the presence of the Crowned Heads and Nobility of Europe,<br>\n        and before large and intelligent assemblages throughout the civilized World. Their profoundly\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"powers-container\">\n        <span class=\"hand\">&#9758;</span>\n        <span class=\"powers-text\">MYSTERIOUS POWERS</span>\n        <span class=\"hand\">&#9756;</span>\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"text-block\">\n        Have astonished the wisest of all countries, and the most learned have been forced by overwhelming evidence to acknowledge<br>\n        them as inexplicable. No complicated or glittering apparatus for deception used.<br>\n        <span class=\"indent\"></span>Notwithstanding the absurd and extravagant pretentions of various mountebanks and imitators, the Davenport Wonders still<br>\n        remain as profound a Mystery as ever.\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"challenge text-center\">CHALLENGE !</div>\n    \n    <div class=\"text-block\">\n        <span class=\"indent\"></span>These gentlemen challenge all Exposers including Baldwin, Bishop and Kellog, also Prof. Keller: none of whom dare meet<br>\n        them<span class=\"large-space\"></span>The following Startling Wonders and Mysterious Movements are all produced in the\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"light text-center\">LIGHT,</div>\n    \n    <div class=\"text-block\">\n        <em>and positively in full view of the entire audience.</em> Musical Instruments are made to play in the most extraordinary manner, and in<br>\n        the most profound and mysterious way. Human hands and arms become visible, and many other interesting experiments are pre-<br>\n        sented, originating only with the Davenport Brothers in the year 1855, and never produced with success by imitators. Every opportunity<br>\n        will be given for the closest inspection by the public and press of this city Skeptics are especially invited to be present and occupy front<br>\n        seats. Come and see for yourselves; take no one's word. Examine and believe your own eyes, be guided by your own reason, as all of<br>\n        the above, through ignorance and superstition, has been attributed to WITCHCRAFT and DEMONOLOGY.\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"caption\">\n        PORTION OF POSTER ADVERTISING IRA E. DAVENPORT'S ENTERTAINMENT AFTER<br>\n        THE DEATH OF HIS BROTHER, W. H. DAVENPORT. \"PROF. J. F. DAY\" WAS<br>\n        A CONJURER WHO ALREADY WAS PERFORMING THE DAVENPORT TRICKS WHEN<br>\n        W. H. DAVENPORT DIED. U.S.A. 1879.\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n</body>\n</html>"
